{"id":"1d7f4605-c0f3-4d09-b5f5-9a4ba7a9f8d2","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"900757189715f7d0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/repo-load.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"ad12e69e91ad164570d008d08803fa0ce6a1ae18","start":3522,"end":3696},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["shell","?.","hub",".","publish","(","\"","project.openFiles","\"",",","{","\"","files","\"",":","projectFiles",",","\"","openEditors","\"",":","pickOpenEditors","(","files",".","map","(","(","file",")","=>","file",".","path",")",".","filter","(","(","path",")","=>","!","path",".","startsWith","(","\"",".git/","\"",")",")",")","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"db3379198bb104f5","after":"ee790c8f88ebff7f"}},"payload":{"text":"A clone's files include its `.git` (git-clone.ts): the workspace becomes the repo, history and all. Editors open\nfrom the working tree only.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:16.216Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:16.216Z"}
{"id":"26fc4789-79ed-4179-948c-73d7ee5fbb7a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"737d38438a5bec5a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/repo-load.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"c83ac86ab4f6813c4d8312623466481b7ddd4994","start":977,"end":1248},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","pickOpenEditors","(","paths",":","string","[]",")",":","string","[]","{","const","preferred","=","paths",".","find","(","(","path",")","=>","/","^readme\\.md$","/","iu",".","test","(","path",")",")","??","paths",".","find","(","(","path",")","=>","/","\\.(?:tsx?|jsx?|html|md)$","/","iu",".","test","(","path",")",")","??","paths","[","0","]",";","return","preferred","!==","undefined","?","[","\"","/workspace/","\"","+","preferred","]",":","[","]",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"6cb8943758141281","after":"303e803af50049c7"}},"payload":{"text":"Pick a file to focus after loading a repo: a top-level README, else the first source/markup file, else the first\nfile — so the load is immediately visible. Paths are repo-relative; the caller has rooted them under /workspace.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:22.477Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:22.477Z"}
{"id":"58101c91-c35d-4269-9fae-3c28a4e2d2c2","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"9ce96d15ef2fb7a5","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/repo-load.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"0c8daf545745b9bdd416e88af9f3963cb452d363","start":4687,"end":5536},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["async","function","fromAddress","(","rpc",":","ShellContext","[","\"","rpc","\"","]",")",":","Promise","<","void",">","{","await","signInSettled",";","const","locks","=","typeof","navigator","===","\"","undefined","\"","?","undefined",":","(","navigator","as","Navigator","&","{","\"","locks","\"","?",":","LockManager","}",")",".","locks",";","if","(","locks","===","undefined",")","{","await","fromAddressNow","(","rpc",")",";","return",";","}","const","ran","=","await","locks",".","request","(","`","editor.repo-load","${","instance","===","undefined","?","\"","","\"",":","`",".","${","instance","}","","`","}","","`",",","{","\"","ifAvailable","\"",":","true","}",",","async","(","lock",")","=>","{","if","(","lock","===","null",")","{","return","false",";","}","await","fromAddressNow","(","rpc",")",";","return","true",";","}",")",";","if","(","!","ran","&&","envRepo","(",")","!==","undefined",")","{","githubLog",".","info","(","\"","another tab is loading into this workspace: this one waits for a reload","\"",")",";","shared",".","set","(","{","\"","githubOpen","\"",":","true","}",")",";","state",".","set","(","{","\"","error","\"",":","\"","Another tab of the editor is loading a repository into this workspace. Reload this tab once it's done to see it here.","\"","}",")",";","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"303e803af50049c7","after":"594843a3cd48a9e6"}},"payload":{"text":"An `env/<owner>/<repo>` address opens that repo, once the app listens — after a sign-in this page finishes, so a\nprivate one is read signed in. The workspace already being that repo's (a reload) keeps it, and the edits made in\nit. The GitHub popover opens over the load, to show it going and say what went wrong (it closes on success). Only a\nworkspace that's no repository's clone is replaced from the address. One the workspace couldn't say (unanswered) is\nkept, as is another repository's clone, which asks: either may hold work not pushed anywhere.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:09.741Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:09.741Z"}
{"id":"62dff563-2ac4-46e8-a401-fe5d95da846a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b8c43b8ee9a936de","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/repo-load.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"9d10b38f9995ef1dfae3e86349ec8dac9888ff9a","start":2642,"end":2694},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["let","files",":","{","\"","path","\"",":","string",";","\"","bytes","\"",":","Uint8Array","}","[]"]},"context":{"before":"58d1ad3d7a630e5b","after":"d6fa2715a9607af3"}},"payload":{"text":"Clone it — one shallow pack, through the API's proxy when signed in (git-clone.ts) — rather than read it blob by\nblob through the API, which fido's limiter holds to 100 requests a minute. The API is the fallback.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:18.366Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:18.366Z"}
{"id":"6a508758-27a8-471a-b389-8d3aafbada20","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3f3aa448355650f9","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/repo-load.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"19bc180063d6b8c3628693b1a28e9b2e7bacd154","start":4096,"end":4188},"shape":{"type":"CallExpression","atoms":["shell","?.","hub",".","publish","(","\"","session.event","\"",",","{","\"","name","\"",":","\"","repo.loaded","\"",",","\"","detail","\"",":","`","","${","owner","}","/","${","repo","}","","`","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"ee5073e8bb4d1c34","after":"501d2a24c40dcf24"}},"payload":{"text":"(the session timeline's, shell/reporting.ts)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:12.207Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:12.207Z"}
{"id":"75fe1621-d443-4f99-a6e7-a924f1896e3a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"779b9e943e48c349","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/repo-load.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"252d54526833e03ef784775d5a0516e30de32e58","start":31,"end":90},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","ShellContext",",","ShellFeature","}","from","\"","./feature","\""]},"context":{"after":"6dd6afe37153e791"}},"payload":{"text":"Loading a GitHub repository into the workspace: the SHELL fetches the files (the token stays here) and publishes them\nto the app over the hub (`project.openFiles`), which writes them into zen-fs, rooted under /workspace. From the GitHub\npopover's Load section, or from the address (`env/<owner>/<repo>`). github.ts is lazy, so fido loads only when a\nrepository is actually fetched.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:26.389Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:41:26.389Z"}
